   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to including\ncertain lands used in single operation for the production of tree nuts in the\ndefinition of agricultural land",
    "basePrintNo": "S6185",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6185-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §301, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6185\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to includ-\ning certain lands used in single operation for the production of tree\nnuts in the definition of agricultural land\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill clarifies the definition of fruit in agricultural and markets\nlaw to be inclusive of tree nuts, and clarifies that land used to\nproduce tree nuts for sale could qualify for agricultural assessments.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends paragraph b of subdivision 2 of section 301 of the\nagriculture and markets law to define fruits to be inclusive of tree\nnuts.\n\nSection 2: Amends subdivision 4 of section 301 of the agriculture and\nmarkets law to include land used to grow tree nuts, including land used\nto grow tree nuts in years one through six before the trees may reason-\nably produce a crop, to be included in the definition of land used in\nagricultural production.\n\nSection 3: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAgricultural assessors may determine the viability of an agricultural\noperation when determining if land qualifies for an agricultural assess-\nment and related tax benefits. While existing agriculture and markets\nlaw clarifies that fruits of any kind are qualifying crops for agricul-\ntural assessments, confusion has been reported regarding the eligibility\nof tree nuts specifically. Tree nuts fall within the botanical defi-\nnition of fruits, and the language of this law shall be amended to\nreflect this fact and avoid any further and future delay in agricultural\nassessments for our tree nut farmers.\n\nTree nuts are also notably slow to grow and bear a marketable quantity\nof fruit. Therefore, an additional section of the law must be updated to\nensure that land growing young tree nut orchards for the purpose of\ncommercial sale may also qualify for an agricultural assessment.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
